WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:07.290
- [Interviewer] All right, Damian.

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.420
- Yes sir.
- [Interviewer] Damian.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.681
So nice to see you this morning.

00:00:09.681 --> 00:00:10.750
- Good to see you too.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:13.730
- [Interviewer] Saw you strolling
by with your shopping cart

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.300
full of recycling stuff.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.310
- [Damian] Yeah.

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:18.570
- [Interviewer] And you told
me some very interesting news.

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:22.600
- [Damian] Yeah. Yeah. I'm
going on four months clean now.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.560
- [Interviewer] So you kicked fentanyl?

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.800
- Yep. And heroin too.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.450
Yeah. Oh, I got the great
help of these though.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.280
I got to put these out,
just to let the world know

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:38.280
that these are available to
them free all day, you know?

00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:42.690
And they help tremendously.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:43.523
- [Interviewer] What are these?

00:00:43.523 --> 00:00:44.670
- Suboxone.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.710
- [Interviewer] Oh yeah. Well, I guess...

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:50.230
So you are using Suboxone?
- Yeah.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:54.950
I kicked cold turkey for it
to resonate and stick with me.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.850
You know, the horribleness of it.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.780
- [Interviewer] Yeah.
- But then afterwards,

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:01.970
cause I have all these prosthetic parts,

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:05.580
I took that just for
pain reliever, you know?

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.580
And also it acts as a, almost
like an inhibitor you know

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.203
from me doing more dope
because if I was to do dope,

00:01:15.203 --> 00:01:17.380
whether fentanyl or heroin,

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.190
it just wouldn't get me high at all.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:20.023
- [Interviewer] Okay so I thought

00:01:20.023 --> 00:01:20.856
when you told me you went cold turkey,

00:01:20.856 --> 00:01:22.300
I just figured you went
cold turkey and quit

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.870
and that was it. But
you're using Suboxone,

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:25.362
which I guess is very helpful, right?

00:01:25.362 --> 00:01:26.330
- Yeah.
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:28.000
A lot of people do.
- I use the Suboxone

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.880
for my prosthetic knee,
metal hand, metal jaw,

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:34.500
metal eye socket, back problem and stuff.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.820
- [Interviewer] How's it feel
to be clean from fentanyl?

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.140
- Good.
- [Interviewer] Yeah?

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:42.756
- I noticed I got quite a
lot of time on my hands.

00:01:42.756 --> 00:01:44.900
(Damian laughs)
Now that I'm not doing

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:48.850
the 24/7 dope search, you know?

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:49.710
- [Interviewer] Right.
- Like, you know,

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.180
I don't have to hustle for dope money,

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:54.290
I don't have to go and find the dope man

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:57.460
once I get the dope money, you know.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.823
That consumed pretty much all...

00:02:00.823 --> 00:02:03.600
- [Interviewer] How many
years were you using?

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.660
- Altogether like 25 years.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.270
- [Interviewer] 25 years.
And how old are you now?

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:09.570
- 43.
- [Interviewer] 43.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:13.920
You've been clean four months?

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.510
- Yeah.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:16.460
- [Interviewer] It's a
lot. That's enough time

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:19.020
to like be able to look back
at that period of your life.

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:22.597
Like what are your thoughts
on that period of addiction?

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.600
- I don't enjoy looking
back on it, you know?

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:36.600
Cause I mean, it's like all
the stuff that I did to get it.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:41.380
I mean I wouldn't do it.
Other people do, you know,

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:45.140
sell themselves and I don't steal.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.600
But I mean I gotta dig through
trash cans for recycling

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:52.470
or I was a panhandling, holding a sign.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:56.517
And that of itself is
horrible. You know what I mean?

00:02:56.517 --> 00:02:59.880
You get these people driving
by just cursing you out,

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.120
telling you to get a job.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:06.120
And they got all of these
great smart ass ways of like...

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.140
- [Interviewer] As if you don't
have enough shame already.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.000
- Yeah. Socking it to you, you know?

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.560
They're like, "Hey, come here
bro. I got something for you.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.650
You hungry?"

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:15.483
I'm like, "Yeah."

00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:16.900
They're like, "Come here, hurry up bro.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:18.180
Light's going to change."

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:20.207
I'll go hobble over. And they're like,

00:03:20.207 --> 00:03:22.980
"Here you go bro. Don't
spend it all on one place."

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.243
Give me two pennies.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.447
- [Interviewer] Really?
- I'm like,

00:03:27.447 --> 00:03:30.672
"I guess it's better
than nothing. Thank you."

00:03:30.672 --> 00:03:33.510
And they're like "Ah
ha ha." Like, you know,

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:36.300
they just had the greatest
laugh of their life, you know,

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.450
for totally disgracing somebody

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.333
and making them feel like crap.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.820
- [Interviewer] No, I think,
I think this little world,

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:45.160
this addiction world,

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.060
is very misunderstood by a lot of people.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.680
- Yeah.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.450
- [Interviewer] So where
are you staying now?

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:51.490
- In a tent.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:52.900
- [Interviewer] You're in a tent?

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.600
But you're not using, you're
surrounded by drug addicts.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.530
- Yeah. Everywhere.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.070
- [Interviewer] Suboxone is...

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.973
What are the ups and downs of Suboxone?

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:02.843
- The ups.

00:04:02.843 --> 00:04:07.843
It helps keep me off of dope, you know

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:11.030
because I know that it's
not gonna have any effect.

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:13.890
If I wanted to do dope, I'd
have to stay clean off of it

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:16.700
for at least five days, you know?

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:21.043
And by then the itch would be way gone.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:25.410
But then I'm going to slowly
start weaning myself off.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.020
I'm not planning on staying on that

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:29.177
for an extended period of time.

00:04:29.177 --> 00:04:30.290
- [Interviewer] And that's legal?

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:31.630
- Yeah.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.350
- [Interviewer] Could
you, if you wanted to,

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:35.010
get a full-time job

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:39.323
and on Suboxone?
- If I got an ID, yeah.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.413
Yeah.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:49.350
- It's classified as a
narcotic but I would think,

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:55.853
well, I don't know actually.
I'm not really sure.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:05:01.810
I mean, I hear that people
have and they do work on it,

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.460
but truthfully I'm not 100% sure.

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:08.920
You know? Cause I mean it says,

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:10.500
don't operate heavy machinery.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.160
- [Interviewer] No, but
if you need to get a job

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.360
at a grocery store or something like that,

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.440
you could do that?
- Oh yeah. Yeah.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.210
- [Interviewer] Is that in
the cards for you? You think?

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:21.480
- Once I get my ID. But that's
not so much in the cards

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.680
as in me getting my own business started

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.620
with the Sober Living Home.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.453
- [Interviewer] Oh really?

00:05:26.453 --> 00:05:27.950
So tell me what you are going to do.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:30.530
- Well, I'm waiting to get my stimulus

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.390
so that I can travel to Arizona,

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:35.670
where I used to stay for a little bit.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:40.210
And I'm gonna cash out
all my 401ks out there.

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:45.193
Through Macy's, Dillard's,
Texaco, Chevron,

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:50.143
Make Modeling Year, Shasta
pools, Whitewater pools,

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.574
a couple other places.

00:05:54.574 --> 00:05:56.880
- [Interviewer] Then
start a sober living thing

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:58.077
to help others?
- Yeah.

00:05:58.077 --> 00:05:59.600
- [Interviewer] Good for you.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:04.600
- And then I'd like to
expand to a rehab if I could.

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:07.090
But that is going to take
me a little bit of time.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:12.090
I researched it and I have to
attend school to be certified

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.950
to be a substance abuse counselor.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:21.400
And then from there then
I could open up a rehab.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.233
- [Interviewer] Good for you.

00:06:22.233 --> 00:06:23.360
- Oh yeah.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:28.050
I figured I'd have the
like edge on helping people

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.774
seeing as how I've been through it all.

00:06:29.774 --> 00:06:30.657
- [Interviewer] Oh I
think you can help others.

00:06:30.657 --> 00:06:34.330
And I bet you it would help your whole.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:37.020
The way you view yourself
by helping other people.

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.840
- Yeah. I mean, I'm slowly like

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:43.117
viewing myself a little bit
better than I was, you know?

00:06:43.117 --> 00:06:44.520
- [Interviewer] No, I can sense that,

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:45.667
when you first walked up, I'm like,

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:48.930
"Wow, that's Damian."
(interviewer laughs)

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:51.840
- Tremendously lost weight but
I mean, I'll get that back.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.870
- [Interviewer] Yeah,
you're always lean anyway.

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:53.710
- Yeah.

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:55.190
- [Interviewer] But now
I can see it in your face

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:56.850
and the way you speak and
your eyes and everything,

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.360
you seem a little clearer and healthier.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:01.890
- Yeah. I mean I feel a lot better.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.161
- [Interviewer] So tell me about

00:07:03.161 --> 00:07:05.050
what it's like to go cold
turkey off of heroin or...

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:08.760
- Oh fentanyl. Ooh, horrible.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:13.440
I mean, it's like worse
than heroin and longer too,

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:15.180
you know?
- [Interviewer] First off,

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:17.270
what's the difference
between heroin and fentanyl?

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.103
You've done both right?

00:07:18.103 --> 00:07:20.670
- Yeah. As far as in the high?

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:23.353
- [Interviewer] No, I guess
the high and the addiction

00:07:23.353 --> 00:07:24.186
and the...
- And the

00:07:24.186 --> 00:07:25.410
addiction withdrawals?

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:29.197
Okay. Well the high,
heroin is not as strong.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:38.613
But when I initially started it,

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:44.170
it hit me pretty, pretty good.

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:46.960
But with me, my chemistry
is like a little mixed up.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:51.560
So I would get hyper for the most part.

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:54.490
And when I do heroin, I'd
be out and about, you know,

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:57.240
just all over the place.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.700
And just to put it into perspective,

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.693
when I was doing speed, methamphetamines,

00:08:04.954 --> 00:08:07.490
I get tired and I go to sleep.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:08.790
- [Interviewer] Yeah.
I think all these drugs

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:10.170
affect each person differently.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.003
- Yeah.

00:08:11.003 --> 00:08:11.836
- [Interviewer] For most people

00:08:11.836 --> 00:08:13.090
I think meth keeps them up right?

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:17.280
- Yeah. But then like I've
been running into people though

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:22.280
such as myself, that it gets
them like tired, you know?

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:27.172
Cause our chemistry, I
think cause I'm ADHD.

00:08:27.172 --> 00:08:28.005
- [Interviewer] Yeah. I
think that's got a lot

00:08:28.005 --> 00:08:29.399
to do with it.
- Yeah.

00:08:29.399 --> 00:08:34.399
And fentanyl, when
fentanyl hit the stage...

00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:41.020
Yeah wow, it was a
different world you know.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:42.850
I didn't have to shoot up

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:46.660
and I could take like one
or two hits of this stuff.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:48.750
You know, when I first started mind you.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.950
And I'd be lit, you know.

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:56.950
Like I would be like, at first
I'd be like just comatose.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:59.940
Like how I would normally
be off of heroin.

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:04.940
But then once my body got, I
guess acclimated to it all,

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:09.873
I started to get the energy
and hyper off of it too.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:14.370
Like I'd see people and it frustrated me,

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:18.700
cause I'd see somebody.
I'd smoke with them.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.083
I'd give them one hit,

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:23.710
next thing I know I'm
having to give them Narcan,

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:25.390
I'm having to breathe for them

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:26.850
cause they're dying in front of me.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:28.042
- [Interviewer] Fentanyl
is a very dangerous drug.

00:09:28.042 --> 00:09:29.878
- Yeah very dangerous.

00:09:29.878 --> 00:09:33.270
And so I'm like, "Okay."

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:35.797
I revive them and I'm like thinking,

00:09:35.797 --> 00:09:38.890
"Cool this is gonna
get me high as hell to.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:41.400
One hit just put this dude out.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:43.577
And he does as much as I do."

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.540
I'd take like 30 or 40 hits

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:50.680
and get nowhere near what
that person got, you know?

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:54.143
And I'm like, it was kind
of frustrating, you know?

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:59.323
Yeah. Cause I mean, my
body, it's something else.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:06.340
I mean, to say the very
least it's very strong.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:08.670
I mean, it's gotten me
this far so far, you know.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:13.670
And I mean I'm blessed, but it
uses substances differently.

00:10:19.451 --> 00:10:24.230
Like once I initially do it,

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.630
after that first time it's like,

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:28.157
body's like already saying like,

00:10:28.157 --> 00:10:30.160
"All right, you're going
to have to up the dose.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:32.320
You're going to have to
do a heck of a lot more.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.071
Get some stronger shit you know."

00:10:34.071 --> 00:10:35.180
(Damian laughs)
- [Interviewer] With fentanyl?

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:36.013
- Yeah.

00:10:36.013 --> 00:10:36.846
- [Interviewer] That's incredible.

00:10:36.846 --> 00:10:37.679
- Yeah.

00:10:37.679 --> 00:10:38.530
- [Interviewer] I've never heard that.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:42.910
- Yeah. I'd be using like just a lot

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.160
in comparison to everybody else.

00:10:45.160 --> 00:10:47.270
- [Interviewer] And so tell
me about going cold turkey.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:50.730
- Oh yeah. So I did cold
turkey on the heroin.

00:10:50.730 --> 00:10:51.923
That was horrible.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:57.760
Stomach upset, diarrhea,
throwing up, cold sweats.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:02.310
Fentanyl is pretty much the
same, only more intense.

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:04.010
- [Interviewer] And how
long does this go on?

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:06.793
- It took me like two, three weeks.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:10.450
Like solid two or three weeks, you know,

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:13.743
of like just feeling like shit you know.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:15.990
- [Interviewer] I've heard it described by

00:11:15.990 --> 00:11:17.508
a lot of heroin or fentanyl addicts

00:11:17.508 --> 00:11:20.203
that dying is preferable.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:25.890
- Yeah. Like I was sitting there

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:28.667
and I would like be
saying out loud, you know,

00:11:28.667 --> 00:11:33.290
"Why can't you just kill me,
God? I don't want to be alive."

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.740
And I was meaning every bit of it too

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:39.920
because I mean when every
single cell in your body

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.160
is screaming out in pain

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:44.287
and just saying "Stop this."

00:11:45.137 --> 00:11:49.020
And I mean, wow, it's something else.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:53.400
And then all the previous
pain that I have normally,

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.723
gets magnified like 100 fold.

00:11:56.822 --> 00:11:59.563
So it's like, I could get
like a paper cut and just,

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:01.970
I mean if I was dope sick you know,

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:04.310
I'd be on the ground balling
pretty much, you know.

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:07.337
Like, "Ah this paper cuts killing me."

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:11.170
And it was like, it would really feel like

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:13.693
it was that horrible, you know?

00:12:14.690 --> 00:12:19.690
So quite a doozy though.
Quite a ride I'll tell you.

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:20.533
- [Interviewer] Well, I'm excited

00:12:20.533 --> 00:12:22.000
that you're considering a sober living

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.973
or your rehab thing for others.

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:29.730
- I mean it's something that
I think is gonna help me

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:34.730
to stick with the proper path, you know?

